From 8baa3b80a659d68c6ba861aea398f1030367c3ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 14 May 2026 15:27:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf phase 11 patch 0141 -- wave-46 Phase 10.5 OPL3
 patch-bank loader

Per flush-instr's docs/internal/WAVE-44-OPL3-LOG-ANALYSIS.md sec. 6.2:
the 8-patch family-bucket placeholder in MidiBackendOpl3 doesn't cover
the dense GM program-change usage in org2mid v1/v2 output -- some
programs map to audibly-wrong patches when collapsed into 7 distinct
buckets. Operator real-HW report (sec. 6.1): PLAY3 + PLAY4 Shack-entry
MIDI "stops" at scene transition because vivi.mid's high-program
events (>= bucket 8 reed/pipe; >= bucket 11 synth-pad on the dense
v1/v2 layout) collapse to family buckets that don't match the SBI
patches in the placeholder bank.

Implement the Phase 10.5 runtime patch-bank loader path that was
already referenced in the existing 8-patch placeholder's banner
("Phase 10.5 may swap in a fuller community bank via runtime
data/opl3-patches.dat loader when operator listening identifies
tracks needing better timbre"). This patch ships the LOADER ONLY;
the actual .dat data file is a ride-along for a follow-on iter
(operator-listening cycle + bank authoring).

File format data/opl3-patches.dat (binary):
  offset  size  field
  0       8     magic "DOPL3v1\n" (the \n is 0x0A)
  8       1     version 0x01 (rejects higher)
  9       1     num_programs 0..128
  10      2     reserved 0 (forward-compat)
  12      N*12  patches N x 12-byte SBI records

Loader behavior:
- At MidiBackendOpl3 ctor (after SDL_DOSOpl3Detect succeeds),
  _try_load_opl3_patches_dat() tries to fopen the .dat file.
- On absence: LOG_INFO with the expected-fallback narration (no
  warning -- this is the wave-46 ship state).
- On file truncation, wrong magic, unsupported version, num_programs
  out of range, or reserved field nonzero: LOG_WARN with specific
  reason + zero the partial-load buffer + leave loaded_count = 0.
- On success: copy patches into _loaded_patch_bank[128][12]; set
  _loaded_patch_bank_count = N. LOG_INFO with payload size + count.

Per-program patch lookup (_program_to_patch) consults the loaded
bank first: if program < _loaded_patch_bank_count, return the
loaded patch; else fall through to the existing 8-patch family-
bucket switch. Drum channel (MIDI ch 9) always uses PATCH_DRUM
regardless of bank loading.

Memory cost: 128 * 12 = 1536 bytes static when loaded; zero before
loader runs. Negligible.

Backward compat: when .dat is absent (the wave-46 ship state),
behavior is bit-for-bit identical to the pre-patch baseline. The
8-patch placeholder remains the active bank. No fps impact in
either case (lookup is one extra branch; sub-cycle overhead).

Regenerated from current vendor state to fix patch context drift
(team-lead's ASCII-cleanup substitution broke the original patch's
context-line matching; source content unchanged; this re-emits a
byte-exact patch against the current upstream context).

Banner regex for tests/run-gameplay-smoke.sh BANNERS array:
"opl3 backend: opl3-patches\.dat (loaded|not found|invalid|truncated|version mismatch|too many programs)".
---
 src/sound/MidiBackendOpl3.cpp | 193 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 187 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/sound/MidiBackendOpl3.cpp b/src/sound/MidiBackendOpl3.cpp
index 064b19f..302ff86 100644
--- a/src/sound/MidiBackendOpl3.cpp
+++ b/src/sound/MidiBackendOpl3.cpp
@@ -43,9 +43,11 @@
 
 #include "MidiBackendOpl3.h"
 
+#include "../ResourceManager.h"
 #include "../Utils/Logger.h"
 
 #include <cstdint>
+#include <cstdio>
 #include <cstring>
 
 // Cross-vendor extern declarations for SDL/0037+ OPL3 helpers. Same
@@ -182,6 +184,160 @@ static constexpr uint8_t PATCH_DRUM[12] = {
   0x00,
 };
 
+// ============================================================================
+// Patch 0141 (wave 46 Phase 10.5): runtime patch-bank loader
+// ============================================================================
+//
+// Per flush-instr's docs/internal/WAVE-44-OPL3-LOG-ANALYSIS.md sec. 6.2:
+// the 8-patch placeholder above doesn't cover the dense GM program-change
+// usage in org2mid v1/v2 output -- some programs lookup-to-bucket result
+// in audibly-wrong patches (Shack scene MIDI-stop on PLAY3/PLAY4 of
+// wave-44; operator report). The original Phase 10.5 plan called out the
+// runtime-loader hook in the existing banner: "may swap in a fuller
+// community bank via runtime data/opl3-patches.dat loader when operator
+// listening identifies tracks needing better timbre."
+//
+// This patch implements the loader path only. The .dat data file is a
+// ride-along for a follow-on iter (operator-listening + actual bank
+// authoring). If the file is absent at engine init, the loader logs an
+// informational line + falls back to the 8-patch placeholder above
+// (existing behavior preserved bit-for-bit). When the .dat file is
+// present + valid, per-program lookups consult the loaded 128-entry
+// table instead.
+//
+// File format `data/opl3-patches.dat` (binary):
+//   offset  size  field
+//   ------  ----  -----
+//   0       8     magic: ASCII "DOPL3v1\n" (the \n is byte 0x0A)
+//   8       1     version: 0x01 (rejects > 1)
+//   9       1     num_programs: 0..128 (typically 128 for full GM melody)
+//   10      2     reserved: must be 0 (alignment + forward-compat field)
+//   12      N*12  patches: N x 12-byte SBI-style records (same layout as
+//                 the inline PATCH_PIANO et al. above; same byte ordering
+//                 op0/KSL_TL/AR_DR/SL_RR/WS, channel FB_CONN, op1...)
+//   12+N*12       EOF
+//
+// N may be < 128 (partial bank); programs >= N fall back to the 8-patch
+// family bucket. The drum channel (MIDI ch 9) always uses PATCH_DRUM
+// regardless of bank loading -- drums are a separate concern (kit slots
+// by note, not program).
+//
+// Loader behavior:
+//   - At MidiBackendOpl3 ctor (after SDL_DOSOpl3Detect succeeds), try to
+//     fopen data/opl3-patches.dat via ResourceManager::getPath.
+//   - On any failure (file missing, wrong magic, bad version, truncated
+//     header, truncated payload, bad reserved field), LOG_WARN with
+//     specific reason + leave _loaded_patch_bank_count = 0. Engine falls
+//     back to 8-patch placeholder.
+//   - On success, copy patches into _loaded_patch_bank static buffer;
+//     set _loaded_patch_bank_count to the actual N.
+//   - At _program_to_patch lookup time: if program < _loaded_patch_bank_
+//     count, return the loaded patch; else fall back to the existing
+//     8-patch family-bucket lookup.
+//
+// Memory cost: 128 * 12 = 1536 bytes static when loaded; zero when not.
+// Negligible for any DOS target.
+
+// Storage for the loaded bank. Static file-scope, zero-init by default.
+// Indexed directly by GM program 0..127.
+static uint8_t _loaded_patch_bank[128][12];
+static int     _loaded_patch_bank_count = 0;  // 0 = not loaded; loader uses
+                                              // this as both "is-loaded" flag
+                                              // AND ceiling for fallback.
+
+// Try to load data/opl3-patches.dat. Returns true on success (sets
+// _loaded_patch_bank + _loaded_patch_bank_count); false otherwise (state
+// unchanged; engine falls back to 8-patch placeholder).
+static bool _try_load_opl3_patches_dat(void)
+{
+  const std::string path =
+      ResourceManager::getInstance()->getPath(
+          "opl3-patches.dat", false);
+  std::FILE *fp = std::fopen(path.c_str(), "rb");
+  if (!fp)
+  {
+    LOG_INFO("opl3 backend: opl3-patches.dat not found at '{}'; "
+             "falling back to 8-patch placeholder. (This is expected "
+             "in the wave-46 iter -- the .dat data file is ride-along "
+             "for a follow-on iter; the loader path itself is shipping.)",
+             path);
+    return false;
+  }
+
+  // Header: 8 magic + 1 version + 1 num_programs + 2 reserved = 12 bytes
+  uint8_t header[12];
+  if (std::fread(header, 1, sizeof header, fp) != sizeof header)
+  {
+    LOG_WARN("opl3 backend: opl3-patches.dat header truncated "
+             "(< 12 bytes); using 8-patch placeholder.");
+    std::fclose(fp);
+    return false;
+  }
+  static const uint8_t k_magic[8] = {
+    'D', 'O', 'P', 'L', '3', 'v', '1', 0x0A
+  };
+  if (std::memcmp(header, k_magic, 8) != 0)
+  {
+    LOG_WARN("opl3 backend: opl3-patches.dat magic mismatch "
+             "(expected 'DOPL3v1\\n'); using 8-patch placeholder.");
+    std::fclose(fp);
+    return false;
+  }
+  const uint8_t version       = header[8];
+  const uint8_t num_programs  = header[9];
+  const uint8_t reserved_lo   = header[10];
+  const uint8_t reserved_hi   = header[11];
+  if (version != 0x01)
+  {
+    LOG_WARN("opl3 backend: opl3-patches.dat version {} unsupported "
+             "(this build expects v1); using 8-patch placeholder.",
+             (int)version);
+    std::fclose(fp);
+    return false;
+  }
+  if (num_programs == 0 || num_programs > 128)
+  {
+    LOG_WARN("opl3 backend: opl3-patches.dat num_programs={} out of "
+             "range [1..128]; using 8-patch placeholder.",
+             (int)num_programs);
+    std::fclose(fp);
+    return false;
+  }
+  if (reserved_lo != 0 || reserved_hi != 0)
+  {
+    LOG_WARN("opl3 backend: opl3-patches.dat reserved field nonzero "
+             "(forward-compat reject); using 8-patch placeholder.");
+    std::fclose(fp);
+    return false;
+  }
+
+  // Payload: num_programs * 12 bytes.
+  const std::size_t payload_bytes = (std::size_t)num_programs * 12u;
+  if (std::fread(_loaded_patch_bank, 1, payload_bytes, fp) != payload_bytes)
+  {
+    LOG_WARN("opl3 backend: opl3-patches.dat payload truncated "
+             "(expected {} bytes for {} programs); using 8-patch "
+             "placeholder. Loaded buffer NOT used (zeroed via static-"
+             "init guard).",
+             (unsigned long)payload_bytes, (int)num_programs);
+    // Zero the partial-load to prevent half-loaded bank from being used.
+    std::memset(_loaded_patch_bank, 0, sizeof _loaded_patch_bank);
+    std::fclose(fp);
+    return false;
+  }
+  std::fclose(fp);
+
+  _loaded_patch_bank_count = (int)num_programs;
+  LOG_INFO("opl3 backend: opl3-patches.dat loaded {} programs from '{}' "
+           "(v1; {} bytes payload). Per-program GM patches now use the "
+           "runtime bank; programs >= {} fall back to 8-patch family "
+           "bucket. Drum channel (MIDI ch 9) unchanged (uses PATCH_DRUM "
+           "regardless of bank loading).",
+           (int)num_programs, path,
+           (unsigned long)payload_bytes, (int)num_programs);
+  return true;
+}
+
 // GM program (0-127) → patch family. Buckets per GM § standard:
 //   0-7   piano       → PATCH_PIANO
 //   8-15  chrom perc  → PATCH_MALLET
@@ -202,6 +358,15 @@ static constexpr uint8_t PATCH_DRUM[12] = {
 static const uint8_t *_program_to_patch(int program)
 {
   if (program < 0 || program > 127) return PATCH_PIANO;
+
+  // Patch 0141 (wave 46): if a runtime bank is loaded AND covers this
+  // program, return the loaded patch. Otherwise fall through to the
+  // 8-patch family-bucket lookup (existing behavior).
+  if (program < _loaded_patch_bank_count)
+  {
+    return _loaded_patch_bank[program];
+  }
+
   const int bucket = program / 8;
   switch (bucket)
   {
@@ -308,6 +473,15 @@ MidiBackendOpl3::MidiBackendOpl3()
   SDL_DOSOpl3InitChip();
   _ready = true;
 
+  // Patch 0141 (wave 46 Phase 10.5): try to load runtime patch bank
+  // from data/opl3-patches.dat. On absence/failure, falls back to the
+  // 8-patch placeholder above (existing behavior preserved). Banner
+  // narration happens inside the loader; engine doesn't need to log
+  // here. Loader is idempotent on this static state -- safe even if
+  // some future code path constructs a second MidiBackendOpl3 (only
+  // one is constructed today; design contract is singleton-ish).
+  _try_load_opl3_patches_dat();
+
   // Initialize per-MIDI-channel state to GM defaults.
   for (int ch = 0; ch < MIDI_CHANNELS; ++ch)
   {
@@ -316,14 +490,21 @@ MidiBackendOpl3::MidiBackendOpl3()
     _channel_expression[ch] = 127;  // GM default (full-on)
   }
 
+  // Patch 0141 (wave 46): banner narrates whether the runtime bank
+  // loaded successfully. Programs >= _loaded_patch_bank_count fall back
+  // to the 8-patch family-bucket placeholder.
   LOG_INFO("opl3 backend ready (OPL3 detected via Adlib timer-1; "
            "InitChip applied 18 x 2-op layout; voice allocator armed). "
-           "Patch bank: 8-patch placeholder covering GM family "
-           "categories (piano/mallet/organ/guitar/strings/brass/reed/"
-           "pad). Aesthetic note: this placeholder will sound generic-"
-           "FM on real OPL3; Phase 10.5 may swap in a fuller community "
-           "bank via runtime data/opl3-patches.dat loader when "
-           "operator listening identifies tracks needing better timbre.");
+           "Patch bank state: {} (loaded_count={}; programs >= "
+           "loaded_count fall back to 8-patch placeholder covering "
+           "GM family categories piano/mallet/organ/guitar/strings/"
+           "brass/reed/pad). Phase 10.5 path: ship a fuller community "
+           "bank as data/opl3-patches.dat (DOPL3v1 format; 12-byte SBI "
+           "records per GM program; loader at MidiBackendOpl3 ctor).",
+           _loaded_patch_bank_count > 0
+               ? "runtime opl3-patches.dat ACTIVE"
+               : "8-patch placeholder ACTIVE (no opl3-patches.dat loaded)",
+           _loaded_patch_bank_count);
 }
 
 MidiBackendOpl3::~MidiBackendOpl3()
-- 
2.47.3

